     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">one solution to this is that you can plot the tree as normal (so the data and tree axis are all correct) and then flip over the tree similar to Fig 4.3A, in <a href=\"https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter4.html#layouts-of-phylogenetic-tree\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter4.html%23layouts-of-phylogenetic-tree&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482227599000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3fLyU6JM2cCWiw7Wj9CZui\">https://yulab-smu.github.io/treedata-book/chapter4.html#layouts-of-phylogenetic-tree</a></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
