    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Pedro,</div><div><br></div><div>You just followed the script found <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msg/bioc-ggtree/wuAlY9phL9Q/L7efezPgDAAJ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msg/bioc-ggtree/wuAlY9phL9Q/L7efezPgDAAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482227599000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1UJ4msAzqBK0w_1akLM3_R\">HERE?</a> I tried that and got some weird results the first time. And Yu said that they might not be right (though I don&#39;t understand why). <br></div><div><br></div><div>If you got it to work using tree_theme2() then I will work on is some more and see if I can get it to work. <br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks!<br><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"><br></span></div></code><br></div><br>On Wednesday, June 5, 2019 at 10:25:16 PM UTC-5, Pedro Senna wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello Jon,</div><div><br></div><div>the way i found to avoid this problem was to extract the 95 HPD height values and use geom_segment() to create new ones, like the example you posted in your previous post. </div><div><br></div><div><br></div><br>Em segunda-feira, 3 de junho de 2019 14:02:09 UTC-4, jonnations  escreveu:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi Everyone,</div><div><br></div><div>I realize there have been a few posts on this topic, <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!searchin/bioc-ggtree/height_0.95_HPD%7Csort:date/bioc-ggtree/4DdgTc1ZL2U/65P6dWYLAwAJ\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!searchin/bioc-ggtree/height_0.95_HPD%257Csort:date/bioc-ggtree/4DdgTc1ZL2U/65P6dWYLAwAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482227599000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3SETusI8ULhZDqWulDnZnl\">HERE</a> for example, but I still haven&#39;t seen an answer that works for my problem. I am plotting a time-calibrated BEAST2 tree with `height_0.95_HPD` values at the nodes. I am reversing the axis using `revts()`. When I do this, the x-axis reverses, but the height_0.95_HPD values do not reverse. See reproducible example below. If you look closely you can see that the node height values do not reverse. <br></div><div><br></div><div>I realize that this may be tricky, but does anyone know how to &quot;reverse&quot; the height_0.95_HPD values before or during plotting? <br></div><div><br></div><div>Thank you very much!</div><div>Jon<br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>example 1</div><div><br></div><div>mac, ggtree version 1.14.6<br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">library</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">ggtree</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br>file </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> system</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">file</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;extdata/BEAST&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;beast_mcc.tree&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">package</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;treeio&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br>beast </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> read</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">beast</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">file</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br><br>ggtr </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> ggtree</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">beast</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> theme_tree2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">()</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">  </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">   geom_range</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">range</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;height_0.95_HPD&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> color</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;red&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">3</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> branch</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">length</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;height&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span st